---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { EMPRESA, ENVIO_GRATIS } from "../data/empresa";
const H = (t: string) => `<span class="hueco">${t}</span>`;
---

<LegalLayout title="Terms of Sale" kicker="LEGAL · TERMS">

  <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
  <p>
    This store is operated by <strong set:html={EMPRESA.nombre.startsWith("[") ? H(EMPRESA.nombre) : EMPRESA.nombre} />,
    registered at <span set:html={EMPRESA.direccion.startsWith("[") ? H(EMPRESA.direccion) : EMPRESA.direccion} />.
    You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${EMPRESA.email}`}>{EMPRESA.email}</a>. In these terms,
    "we" and "us" mean that company, and "you" means the person placing an order.
  </p>
  <p>
    By placing an order you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please do not order.
  </p>

  <h2>What we sell</h2>
  <p>
    We sell Rabbit Fuel, a caffeinated soft drink made with yerba mate and guaraná, and merchandise
    such as The Lookout plush and The Zoomies towel. We also offer The Burrow, a monthly membership
    described in its own section below.
  </p>
  <p>
    Product photographs are as accurate as we can make them. Colours can look different from one
    screen to another, and small variations in textile and print are normal and are not defects.
  </p>

  <h2>Rabbit Fuel: who should not drink it</h2>
  <p>
    Rabbit Fuel contains caffeine from natural sources. It is <strong>not recommended for children,
    pregnant or breastfeeding people, or anyone sensitive to caffeine</strong>. It is a drink, not a
    medicine or a supplement, and it is not intended to diagnose, treat or prevent anything. If you
    have a medical condition, ask a health professional before drinking it.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and payment</h2>
  <p>
    All prices are shown in US dollars. Taxes and duties, where they apply, are calculated at
    checkout or charged on delivery, depending on the destination.
  </p>
  <p>
    Payments are processed by <strong>Stripe</strong>. We never see or store your full card number.
    Placing an order is an offer to buy; the contract is formed when we confirm your order by email.
    If we cannot fulfil an order, we will tell you and refund you in full.
  </p>
  <p>
    We try hard to keep prices accurate. If an item is listed at an obviously wrong price, we may
    cancel the order and refund you rather than fulfil it, and we will tell you why.
  </p>

  <h2>The Burrow: membership terms</h2>
  <p>
    The Burrow is a <strong>monthly membership that renews automatically</strong> until you cancel it,
    at the price of the plan you chose.
  </p>
  <p>
    We bill on a <strong>single monthly cut-off, not on your own join date</strong>. Members are
    charged at the start of each month and the boxes go out together in the first week, so that
    everyone receives that month's card at roughly the same time. If you join mid-month, you are
    charged once when you join — that payment covers your first box, which ships with the next
    cut-off — and from then on you are charged at the start of each month. You are never charged
    twice for the same box, and we tell you your first box date when you subscribe.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You can pause once a year, and we hold your card.</strong> That month you are not charged and no box goes out, but your copy of that month's card is reserved and travels with the next one. Your collection does not break. One pause per year, not unlimited.</li>
    <li>You can <strong>cancel at any time</strong> from <strong>MY BURROW</strong> in your account, or by writing to <a href={`mailto:${EMPRESA.email}`}>{EMPRESA.email}</a>. The cancellation takes effect at the end of the period you have already paid for. We do not charge a cancellation fee.</li>
    <li>A box that has already been prepared or shipped for the current period is not refunded by cancelling, but you may return it under our <a href="/returns">returns policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The annual plan</strong> ($319 Curious, $539 Digger) is a single payment that covers
      twelve monthly boxes — you pay for eleven and the twelfth is on us. It renews once a year,
      and we email you before it does, with time to cancel. Cancelling an annual plan stops the
      renewal: the boxes of the year you already paid for keep arriving until that year ends.</li>
    <li>If we change the price of a plan, we will tell you by email before it affects you, with enough notice to cancel first.</li>
    <li>Collectible cards, stickers and limited items included with a membership are part of that month's box. Once a month has passed, that month's card is not reprinted and cannot be bought separately.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Delivery, returns and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Delivery times, costs and the free-shipping threshold of ${ENVIO_GRATIS} are set out in our
    <a href="/shipping">shipping policy</a>. Your right to return items and how refunds work are set
    out in our <a href="/returns">returns and refunds policy</a>. Both pages form part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You need an account to order and to use The Burrow. Accounts are handled by Clerk, our
    authentication provider; we never see your password. Keep your login details to yourself — you
    are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us straight away if you think someone
    else has access to it.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may suspend or close an account that is used for fraud, abuse, or to resell our products
    without our agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>What belongs to us</h2>
  <p>
    The SnackRabbit name, the rabbit mark, the artwork on the cards, the photographs and the texts on
    this site belong to us. You may share and post them as a customer; you may not use them to sell
    anything, to make merchandise, or to suggest that we endorse something we do not.
  </p>

  <h2>Our responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    We are responsible for delivering what you bought, in the condition described. We are not
    responsible for losses that we could not reasonably have foreseen, or for things outside our
    control such as strikes, extreme weather, or a carrier losing a parcel after we handed it over —
    although in that last case we will still resolve it with you, as described in our shipping policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms takes away rights that the law gives you as a consumer and that cannot be
    signed away.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of
    <span set:html={EMPRESA.jurisdiccion.startsWith("[") ? H(EMPRESA.jurisdiccion) : EMPRESA.jurisdiccion}/>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The version that applies to your order is the one published on the day
    you placed it, and the date at the top of this page tells you when it last changed.
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
